{
  "id": "editor-compare",
  "title": "A held seat frame supports split, wipe and difference views while measurements read the live root",
  "binding": "Both legs place the existing editor-grid scene in an inset seat at (0.125, 0.125), with 0.75 width and height, preserving its aspect and exposing an incorrect source crop origin. They use that scene and the same requested surface grid. The positive leg enters build mode before holding the grid-free seat; the discriminating leg stays in play mode, so its grid never draws. Each comparison command waits for its ordinary live-root capture before the script continues. Split maps the whole held and live views into the left and right halves; the held platform stays below mean blue 0.18, while the live platform exceeds 0.35 only in build mode. Wipe retains the original left platform and shows the live right ramp above blue 0.22. Absolute difference shows the changed platform above blue 0.25 only in build mode; equal images remain black. The changed-pixel echo uses the shared two-code RGB threshold, and turning comparison off then hiding the grid restores the original image. These broad region bounds follow the editor-grid fixture's existing geometric regions and leave interpolation noise outside the decision. A small authored pipeline also probes the shared filter directly: a 4x4 crop at (2,2) in an 8x8 image has a black guard outside it and red/green steps from codes 64 to 191 inside. Expanded fourfold, pixel (2,8) has red code 75 and green code 191 with cubic crop-clamped taps; reading the outside guard instead gives code 78. The discriminating leg uses bilinear and yields code 80. An exact 4x4 output reads codes 64 and 191 at the crop corners, proving the offset fast path.",
  "bootShape": "offscreen",
  "backends": [
    "vulkan",
    "directx"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "gpu"
  ],
